## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical reasoning on per-tenant quotas, config hot-reload via Docker Config, and lightweight canary routing in a docker-dca cluster.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for runtime config delivery
- Lightweight sidecar pattern for per-tenant quotas
- Token-bucket rate limiting per tenant
- Canary routing and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simplified quota sidecar sketch (pseudo)
const quotas = loadYamlFromConfig('quotas.yaml');
let buckets = {};

function handle(req, res, next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Tenant required');
  const q = quotas[tenant] || quotas.default;
  const now = Date.now();
  let b = buckets[tenant] || { tokens: q.limit, last: now };
  const elapsed = Math.max(0, now - b.last);
  b.tokens = Math.min(q.limit, b.tokens + (elapsed * (q.refillRate || 1)));
  b.last = now;
  if(b.tokens < 1){ return res.status(429).send('Quota exceeded'); }
  b.tokens -= 1;
  buckets[tenant] = b;
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test quota correctness across tenants?
- How would you handle config validation errors and rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to wire config-driven per-tenant controls in a multi-DC docker-dca setup, with TLS edge and simple runtime enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for runtime limits
- Per-tenant rate limiting (token bucket)
- TLS via Traefik edge proxy
- Basic cross-DC deployment considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: token bucket per tenant with 60 rpm
const limits = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/etc/config/tenant-rate-limits.json','utf8'));
const buckets = new Map();
function allow(tenant){
  const now = Date.now();
  let b = buckets.get(tenant);
  if(!b){ b = {tokens: limits[tenant]||0, last: now}; buckets.set(tenant,b); }
  // simplistic: refill 1 token per second for 60s window
  const elapsed = (now - b.last)/1000; b.last = now; b.tokens = Math.min((limits[tenant]||0), b.tokens + elapsed);
  if(b.tokens >= 1){ b.tokens--; return true; }
  return false;
}
```

